# Usage

Use when the user wants **serialized Sitecore items as YAML** under **`authoring/items/`** for **any** new or updated TSX component—then sync with XM Cloud / Sitecore CLI. **Do not** use Sitecore or Marketer MCP for this workflow.

Keep **`.sitecore/component-map.ts`** (or your app’s component map) aligned with the Json Rendering **`componentName`** value.

---

## 0) Fill the module table once per repo (then reuse)

Replace placeholders for **your** authoring layout. Example values below are for **SitecoreSilver** in this repo.

| Placeholder                 | Meaning                                                                                      | Example (SitecoreSilver)                                                    |
| --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `{{moduleKey}}`             | Top-level folder under `authoring/items/` that holds serialized trees                        | `sitecoresilver`                                                            |
| `{{moduleDefinitionFile}}`  | Module JSON next to `items/` (defines includes / roots)                                      | `authoring/items/sitecoresilver.module.json`                             |
| `{{sitecoreProjectKey}}`    | Sitecore segment in `/templates/Project/…`, `/layout/Renderings/Project/…`, etc.             | `sitecoresilver`                                                            |
| `{{siteKey}}`               | Site folder name under `authoring/items/{{moduleKey}}/site/`                                 | `sitecoresilver`                                                         |
| `{{rootWebsitePath}}`       | Site root item path in Sitecore                                                              | `/sitecore/content/sitecoresilver/sitecoresilver`                                  |
| `{{homeWebsitePath}}`       | Home item path (link standard values)                                                        | `/sitecore/content/sitecoresilver/sitecoresilver/home`                             |
| `{{sitecoreAuthorAccount}}` | User name written to **new** items’ audit fields (`__Owner`, `__Created by`, `__Updated by`) | `sitecore\johan.becue@sitecore.com` (override per environment) |

**Derived paths (always derive from the table—do not hardcode another vertical’s names):**

- `{{serializationRoot}}` = `authoring/items/{{moduleKey}}/`
- **Templates:** `{{serializationRoot}}templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/`
- **Json renderings:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectRenderings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/`
- **Placeholder settings:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectPlaceholderSettings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/`
- **Site content:** `{{serializationRoot}}site/{{siteKey}}/`
- **Available Renderings (EE picker):** `{{serializationRoot}}site/{{siteKey}}/Presentation/Available Renderings/` + the site’s group file (e.g. `SitecoreSilver.yml` when `{{sitecoreProjectKey}}` is `sitecoresilver`—confirm the filename under that folder).

If your module JSON uses different include names, map them from **`{{moduleDefinitionFile}}`** instead of the rows above.

---

## 1) Name the new component (from TSX)

| Placeholder                     | Rule                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| `{{tsxFilePath}}`               | Repo path to the component file, e.g. `industry-verticals/sitecoresilver/src/components/sitecoresilver/MyWidget.tsx`                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| `{{componentMapKey}}`           | Exact string key in the Content SDK **component map** (often the TSX file base name)                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |
| `{{sitecoreBaseName}}`          | Short name for **template folder**, **inner datasource template item**, **Json Rendering item name**, and **`{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder`** template. Often = file base name, or strip a **known brand prefix** (e.g. `SitecoreSilverMyWidget` → `MyWidget`)—**pick one rule per vertical and apply consistently**. |
| `{{dataFolderDisplayName}}`     | Plural (or conventional) **site Data** subfolder for datasource instances                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | e.g. `MyWidgets`        |
| `{{defaultDatasourceItemName}}` | First default item under that folder                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | e.g. `Default MyWidget` |

