## New YAML files: audit / user fields (mandatory)

Whenever you **create** a new serialized item YAML (template, rendering, site Data, placeholder settings, Presentation, etc.), set these fields to **`{{sitecoreAuthorAccount}}`** everywhere they appear on that item (typically under `Languages` → `Versions` → `Fields`, and sometimes alongside other metadata):

| Hint           | Sitecore field id (for YAML `ID:`)     | Value                                                                                  |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `__Owner`      | `52807595-0f8f-4b20-8d2a-cb71d28c6103` | `{{sitecoreAuthorAccount}}` (multiline block string, same style as existing SitecoreSilver YAML) |
| `__Created by` | `5dd74568-4d4b-44c1-b513-0af5f4cda34f` | `{{sitecoreAuthorAccount}}`                                                            |
| `__Updated by` | `badd9cf9-53e0-4d0c-bcc0-2d784c282f6a` | `{{sitecoreAuthorAccount}}`                                                            |

**Rules:**

- Apply on **create** for every new `.yml` file you add (each item’s first version / shared metadata as appropriate—mirror sibling items in the same folder).
- On **update-only** edits to existing YAML, do **not** rewrite `__Created by` unless you are intentionally re-authoring; you may still set **`__Updated by`** to `{{sitecoreAuthorAccount}}` if your team convention bumps it on every edit (default here: **set `__Updated by` on substantive updates**; leave historical `__Created by` unchanged).
- Literal for this SitecoreSilver app: `sitecore\johan.becue@sitecore.com` (backslash + email).

