## Steps → YAML (generic patterns)

In all paths below, substitute **`{{serializationRoot}}`**, **`{{sitecoreProjectKey}}`**, **`{{sitecoreBaseName}}`**, **`{{siteKey}}`**.

### Step 1 — Template folder item

- **Create:** `{{serializationRoot}}templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml`
- **Sitecore `Path:`:** `/sitecore/templates/Project/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}`
- **Clone from:** `{{referenceSitecoreBaseName}}.yml` at the same templates level.

### Step 2 — Datasource template tree

Under `templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}/`:

- Inner template `{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml`, section `Data.yml`, one yml per field, `__Standard Values.yml`
- **Clone** layout from `{{referenceSerializationPrefix}}` (adjust names, IDs, `Parent`).

### Step 3 — Datasource **folder** template

- `{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder.yml` + `{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder/__Standard Values.yml`
- Mirror **`{{referenceSitecoreBaseName}} Folder`** pattern (`__Masters`, icons).

### Step 4 — Rendering parameters template

- `{{sitecoreBaseName}} Parameters.yml`, child `Rendering Parameters.yml`, `__Standard Values.yml`
- Clone from reference **Parameters** tree (base templates: rendering params + dynamic placeholder + rendering id—same as your reference Json rendering component).

### Step 5 — Site Data insert options (if present in YAML)

If the repo serializes the item that controls **Insert Options** under `Data`, append the new **`{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder`** template ID to `__Masters`. If not serialized, state **Step 5 N/A** in the change log.

### Step 6 — Site datasource folder + default item

- `{{serializationRoot}}site/{{siteKey}}/Data/{{dataFolderDisplayName}}.yml`
- `…/Data/{{dataFolderDisplayName}}/{{defaultDatasourceItemName}}.yml`
- **Paths** under `{{rootWebsitePath}}/Data/…`

**`Template` (root-level YAML key on each content item)—must match Sitecore definitions you created; never reuse another component’s template id by mistake.**

| Item you serialize                                                                    | `Template:` value = GUID from …                                                                                                                                                                                                                  |
| ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Data folder** holding datasource instances (e.g. `Data/BoxCards`, `Data/MyWidgets`) | **`{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder`** template item: `{{serializationRoot}}templatesProject/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}} Folder.yml` → use its top-level **`ID:`** (not `LinkBoxCard Folder`, `Common/…`, etc.). |
| **Leaf datasource** under that folder (e.g. a single card or section row)             | **Inner datasource template**: `…/{{sitecoreBaseName}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml` → its **`ID:`** (the template whose fields match the TSX `fields`).                                                                                             |

**Verify:** `Datasource Template` on the Json Rendering points at the inner template **path**; site folder items use **Folder** template id; children use **inner** template id. All three must refer to the **same** `{{sitecoreBaseName}}` tree.

### Step 7 — Json Rendering

- **Create:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectRenderings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml`
- **`componentName`:** `{{componentMapKey}}`
- **Datasource / parameters / location:** same **shape** as reference rendering; replace names and GUIDs with the new template IDs/paths.

### Step 8 — Placeholder settings (only if TSX uses `<Placeholder />`)

- **Create:** `{{serializationRoot}}projectPlaceholderSettings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/<kebab-slug>.yml`
- **Placeholder Key:** TSX pattern with dynamic segment replaced by `{*}` (e.g. `my-widgets-${id}` → `my-widgets-{*}`).
- **Allowed Controls:** Json Rendering IDs allowed in that placeholder.
- **Update** parent rendering(s): **`Placeholders`** shared field lists this placeholder settings item’s ID.

### Step 9 — Available Renderings (Experience Editor component list)

If your site serializes an **Available Renderings** item (so editors can insert Json renderings from a curated list), **update that YAML** whenever you add a new Json Rendering under **`{{serializationRoot}}projectRenderings/{{sitecoreProjectKey}}/`**.

| Detail           | Value                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Typical path** | `{{serializationRoot}}site/{{siteKey}}/Presentation/Available Renderings/<Group>.yml` — use the file that already exists for your site (do not invent a second list unless the product requires it).                                                                                                                                                                             |
| **Shared field** | `{715AE6C0-71C8-4744-AB4F-65362D20AD65}` — `Hint: Renderings`.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |
| **Meaning**      | Sitecore stores a **pipe-separated** list of **Json Rendering item IDs** (each id in braces). Serialized YAML in this repo often shows **one `{GUID}` per line** under a multiline `Value: \|`; that is equivalent to the pipe-separated list—**append** the new rendering’s **`ID`** from `projectRenderings/.../{{sitecoreBaseName}}.yml` in the same format as sibling lines. |
| **Rules**        | Do **not** duplicate GUIDs; preserve existing entries; match brace casing to the file’s convention.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |

If no **Available Renderings** item exists under `Presentation/` for your site, **Step 9 N/A**—note that in the change log.

### Step 10 — Partial designs + page design (site chrome only)

Use when the component is **shared site chrome** (header, footer, global alert bar) that should appear on **every page** without duplicating `__Renderings` on each page item.

**SitecoreSilver reference (clone this pattern):**

| Item | Path under `{{serializationRoot}}site/{{siteKey}}/` |
|------|------------------------------------------------------|
| Partial design | `Presentation/Partial Designs/<name>.yml` — `Signature`, `__Renderings` with `s:ph="headless-header"` or `headless-footer` |
| Partial placeholder | `Presentation/Placeholder Settings/Partial Design/<name>.yml` — `Placeholder Key` = `sxa-header` / `sxa-footer` |
| Page design | `Presentation/Page Designs/DefaultPage.yml` — `PartialDesigns` = pipe-separated partial design **GUIDs** |
| Template mapping | `Presentation/Page Designs.yml` — `TemplatesMapping` links page template → page design |
| Datasource | `Data/<Folder>/<Default Item>.yml` — referenced by `s:ds` on partial design rendering |

**Rules:**

1. **App layout placeholders** (`headless-header`, `headless-main`, `headless-footer`) come from `Layout.tsx` — partial design renderings must use these keys, not `sxa-*`.
2. **`sxa-header` / `sxa-footer`** are **page-design composition** slots only (`Placeholder Settings/Partial Design/`).
3. **Nested components** (Navigation, LinkList) go under **component** placeholders (`sitecoresilver-header-nav-{*}`, etc.) — inside the partial design `__Renderings` (preferred) or on the page under `/headless-header/...`.
4. **Page content** components (hero, grids, promos): add to page `__Renderings` with `s:ph="headless-main"` — **not** in header/footer partial designs.
5. When adding a new partial design, **append its item GUID** to the page design `PartialDesigns` field (pipe-separated).

**Step 10 N/A** for page-specific components — use page `__Renderings` on `headless-main` only.

